From: Ragu Manjegowda <ragu.manjegowda@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: retain direct PTL sensor topology

The external Intel vision-drivers CVS module handles ownership but does not
register a V4L2 subdevice. Treating Panther Lake INTC10E1 as a CSI bridge
therefore leaves the IPU7 async notifier waiting forever and prevents the
OV08X40 sensor from binding.

Keep the pre-7.2 direct sensor-to-IPU topology for the affected CVS IDs while
the external ownership driver remains in use.
---
 drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -168,9 +168,6 @@ static const struct acpi_device_id ivsc_acpi_ids[] = {
 	{ "INTC1095" },
 	{ "INTC100A" },
 	{ "INTC10CF" },
-	{ "INTC10DE" }, /* LNL */
-	{ "INTC10E0" }, /* ARL */
-	{ "INTC10E1" }, /* PTL */
 };
 
 static struct acpi_device *ipu_bridge_get_ivsc_acpi_dev(struct acpi_device *adev)
-- 
2.51.0
